\name{LatticeLayerProcessor}
\alias{LatticeLayerProcessor}
\title{lattice Layer Processor}
\description{
Base class for the processors that read a layer of a lattice panel. A
processor is handed the trellis object, the panel it reads
(\code{panel_ctx}) and the grobs its layer was drawn as (\code{layer_info$grobs}),
and answers the layer as the orchestrator emits it -- or \code{NULL} when its
marks cannot be read, which makes the whole chart fall back to an image.

A layer with nothing drawn in it -- a group with no finite value -- is
answered with empty \code{data}, and the orchestrator leaves it out.

\code{panel_ctx} carries \code{packet}, \code{column} and \code{row} (the layout cell lattice
drew the panel in), \code{args} (the panel's arguments, as its panel function
received them), \code{title}, the packet's \code{x_limits} and \code{y_limits}, and the
chart's \code{group_levels} and \code{group_title}.
}
\keyword{internal}
